                "word": "shillelagh",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "2bdfebef-1d91-47a2-951f-d776a300edb4",
                        "entry_id": "a4f2181e-1116-3cb1-a4af-6ce80c46fc98",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "shillelaghs"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b70a0f12-525d-3457-bce7-0c9a3786fb00",
                        "entry_id": "a4f2181e-1116-3cb1-a4af-6ce80c46fc98",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A wooden (traditionally blackthorn (sloe) wood) club ending with a large knob."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Ireland"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5bba87a2-67b2-4666-86be-1f36d6531489",
                                "sense_id": "b70a0f12-525d-3457-bce7-0c9a3786fb00",
                                "text": "[T]he stem of a stout young oak or ash tree, into the end of which, where the roots had been rounded off, a quantity of molten lead was poured, making the shillelagh more formidable in such hands than a sword would have been – much harder to parry, and impossible to break."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e07c6eac-f446-4e87-8d98-a9df7aa3fbdc",
                                "sense_id": "b70a0f12-525d-3457-bce7-0c9a3786fb00",
                                "text": "It beats all your guns and your rifles, / For it goes off whene'er you desire, / And it's sure to hit just what it aims at, / For shillelaghs they never miss fire."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "611f1a47-d7a7-44c6-8f04-4498f0414afe",
                                "sense_id": "b70a0f12-525d-3457-bce7-0c9a3786fb00",
                                "text": "\"My sorrow!\" cried Toirdealbhach. \"What do I want to be a saint for at all, is my puzzle! If I could fetch one crack at somebody with me ould shillelagh\"—here he produced a frightful-looking weapon from under his gown—\"wouldn't it be better than all the saints in Ireland?\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "74dc4fd5-0cb2-4fe8-8479-728f893aff9b",
                                "sense_id": "b70a0f12-525d-3457-bce7-0c9a3786fb00",
                                "text": "The precise size and shape of a shillelagh can be hard to agree upon, but most of those who have an interest in Irish culture will readily acknowledge that a knobbed stick, made of oak or blackthorn, are the distinguishing characteristics of a shillelagh."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ac64d0b8-e8b9-301d-b1f8-d92f51988cb9",
                        "entry_id": "a4f2181e-1116-3cb1-a4af-6ce80c46fc98",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any cudgel, whether or not of Irish origin."
